+
+## Observable differences found by tests
+
+- LoRA selects: names containing `../` are rejected with ValueError (refused technique: path traversal); the original resolved them.
+- LoRA selects: file metadata is returned as the node's own UI output instead of a server-pushed HTML table (refused technique -> public replacement).
+- Error text: error types are preserved but message text may differ (e.g. a missing model file in Multi/Extra/VACE select); on the ordinary-Guest route errors arrive wrapped as WireError("<Type>: ...") at the transport level.
+- Sampler Settings: text inputs over 64 KiB are rejected (see safety narrowings).
+
+## Deliberate differences
+
+- **`DownloadAndLoadWav2VecModel`: wrong bytes at the pinned name raise (since r12).** The loader asks `assets.exists` before any download, so an installed file with wrong bytes at the pinned name now raises the pin error (`ValueError: Wav2Vec checkpoint differs from the pinned original bundle`) instead of being re-downloaded in-process. Remove the file to re-fetch it. This matches the original's exists-first behaviour: it downloads only when the path is absent (fantasytalking/nodes.py:52-66). Unlike the original, which loads whatever is there, the conversion also checks the pinned size and sha256.
+
+## Known issues
+
+- `WanVideoDiffusionForcingSampler` / staged samplers: if another extension hooks the transformer, release after an error happens when the caller drops the error (torch hook wrappers are library frames; the release helper never writes library cells).
+- Model menus marked PARTIAL (GGUF/`unet_gguf` and `mmaudio` entries) until the host supports pack-declared model folders; 19 schema remote-option routes unchanged (three name folders outside the ModelFolder contract).
+- `WanVideoDecodeOviAudio`: at bf16, separate processes can differ by process-level numeric state (wsl r1: max_abs 0.287 on the waveform, first visible at the VAE decoder output). In one interpreter the converted decoder is bit-exact with the original (cross r1), so this is not converted code. bf16 equality across separate processes is not claimed (see Evidence notes).
+- `WanVideoUniAnimateDWPoseDetector`, `LynxEncodeFaceIP` and `LynxInsightFaceCrop` refuse at dispatch on live: their required weights need models.download, which live withholds even for installed weights (platform request #23).
+- `DownloadAndLoadWav2VecModel` works on live only once the operator stages the pinned weights; absent weights still ask for models.download, which live refuses.
+- `FantasyPortraitFaceDetector` refuses on live: the deployed WAN dependency profile has no ONNX package (request #22; see Evidence notes).
+- `TextImageEncodeQwenVL` and `WanVideoAddBindweaveEmbeds` need SDK207 (Core 708e6c01) and fail on the deployed 0d6ec97e engine: their converted code calls SDK APIs that engine lacks (`LatentRef.samples`, `CondRef.embedding`, and `ClipRef.encode` with images and a template).
+
+## Evidence notes
+
+- `WanVideoDiffusionForcingSampler` error-path release, check 3. r1 (forcing-leakfix-r1, handoff 1e6d4d76..., preserved FAIL) passed unipc parity, Euler error parity and "transformer weakref dead after gc", and FAILED "no retained owner/sampler frames" because that scan ran inside the event-loop step still delivering the error: those frames were held only by asyncio's in-flight Future, not by pack code. r2 (forcing-leakfix-r2, handoff ca91ea43..., same bytes, cases and envelope) redefined check 3 to measure what the fix is about: in that same step the weakref is dead and every live frame holds no owned state (worker frames cleared; owner transformer/pipeline/execution are None), and after the caller drops the error (two loop turns + gc) no package frames remain and the error and transformer are released. r2 passed 25/25. MERVYN accepted the redefinition (m_119fadf146); both runs are kept as evidence.
+- Error release, known gap (sampler-block1-test-r1 error_release, handoff d043baf6..., preserved FAIL). A natural error raised inside the vendored nested closure `predict_with_cfg` matched the original exactly, but the converted transformer stayed alive while the error was in flight: the closure frame keeps its function, whose closure cells hold the sampler's transformer, and clearing frames cannot reach cells. It is freed once the caller drops the error. The forcing sampler shares this pattern (forcing-leakfix-r2 passed because its Euler error is raised outside the closure). A helper that empties each finished traceback frame's own cells (sampler-error-release-r2, static) is the proposed fix for rev 4.
+- Forcing/sampler error release (rev 4): sampler-block1 error_release FAIL (d043baf6) -> fixed by a package-scoped helper that empties the cells of finished frames of this package's own code (never library frames); GO(a): sampler error_release PASS (b71455a9), forcing unipc PASS on final bytes (7d5bc06b), forcing closure-error FAIL preserved (6df74ca1: held in-step by torch's hook wrapper created by OUR harness forward hook); R1 rerun with the observer on transformer.head PASS 16/16 (8865eade). MERVYN ruled out writing library-frame cells (m_32d504a4e7).
+- wav2vec family (wav2vec-d 60062897): stated exclusion - checkpoint directory provenance (_name_or_path); stated tolerance - masked_spec_embed values, which the ORIGINAL loader itself does not determine (two identical original loads from the same RNG state differ; control run recorded).
