+- Sampler experimental/feta (feta-batched r3, COMPARISON `61ec2016`, selection `m_ee23614b11`): closed by reviewed normalization, not passed. Case x3b (bidirectional sampling) raises the original's NoCapableBackendError on both sides with the same type, raising function and file. Its two exact message checks FAIL and stay recorded: one set literal prints in hash-randomized order (original `{torch.float32, torch.float16, torch.bfloat16}`, converted `{torch.bfloat16, torch.float32, torch.float16}`), and PYTHONHASHSEED cannot be pinned under `-I`. Under the reviewed normalization (MERVYN R1 `m_ac4fbd5c7d`: only that single set literal is compared as a sorted list, all other text exactly) both are equal. The x3b exact-message FAIL first seen in feta r2 is kept on record. The feta r1/r2 runs used trees that differed from the staged bytes in six files; r3 supersedes them.
